          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بريد (barīd) is usually traced to Late Latin veredus, \"post-horse\", through Greek beredos (EtymDB), probably by way of Aramaic. Lane's sources call it Persian, from a phrase for the docked tails of post-mules, an account that looks like a folk etymology."
            }
          ]
        },
